   "label": "California Aikido Federation (pre-1974)",
   "canonical_name": "California Aikido Federation",
   "metadata": {
    "asserted_by": "kkron",
    "note": "kkron refers to the 'California Aikido Association' being already in existence before Nadeau's return from Japan, headquartered in Southern California. The Aikido Journal entry for Rod Kobayashi refers to the 'California Aikido Federation' which he led through 1974. This may be the same or a precursor organization. The current CAA (ai-ki-do.org) was formed in 2002 from the AANC (1980), which was preceded by the Northern California Yudansha Kai (1974)."
   },
   "source_urls": [
    "kkron://personal-communication/dojo-origins-caa"
   ]
